# PetSocial Laravel / Livewire Performance Rules

- Target Laravel 13.12.0, Livewire 4.3, PHP 8.5 locally, this app's Composer `^8.4` PHP floor, and Laravel 13's PHP >= 8.3 support floor.
- Use Laravel Boost `application_info` and `search-docs` before changing Laravel or Livewire behavior.
- Prefer official Laravel and Livewire APIs, Laravel-native features, PHP 8.3+ typing, constructor property promotion, readonly values, typed properties, explicit return types, enums, and Laravel-supported PHP attributes where useful.
- Every Eloquent list query must define eager loads, selected parent/relation columns, pagination, deterministic sorting, and aggregate counts or existence flags.
- Keep `Model::preventLazyLoading(! app()->isProduction())` enabled unless a documented and tested exception exists.
- Livewire checklist: prefer single-file components for focused components and multi-file components for complex components; avoid heavy queries in `render()`; keep public properties small, safe, authorized, and serializable; never store large Eloquent collections or sensitive data publicly; use `#[Computed]`, `#[Locked]`, `#[Url]`, `#[Session]`, `#[Lazy]`, `#[Defer]`, `#[Isolate]`, `#[Async]`, `#[Renderless]`, and `@island` only when they improve clarity or performance; use `wire:show` or Alpine for simple show/hide behavior, `wire:navigate` for suitable internal links, stable `wire:key` values in loops, and clear stale computed values after writes.
- Eloquent checklist: start from `Model::query()`; select parent and relation columns explicitly; include relationship keys; use `with()`, `load()`, `loadMissing()`, `withCount()`, `withSum()`, `withExists()`, `withAvg()`, `withMin()`, `withMax()`, `withWhereHas()`, `morphWith()`, and `loadMorph()` deliberately; never run unloaded relationship, count, sum, exists, reaction, save, follow, or policy-adjacent queries inside loops; never use `Model::all()` for pages, tables, exports, queued work, or APIs unless tiny and documented.
- Cache/queue/API checklist: use `Cache::remember()`, `Cache::memo()`, and `Cache::touch()` with explicit keys, TTLs, and invalidation; never use `Cache::flush()` on shared stores; use cache tags only with a supported-driver fallback; move slow work out of HTTP/Livewire into project-approved queued work without creating `app/Jobs`; define queue names, retries, backoff, timeouts, fail-on-timeout, and duplicate-burst protections for `ShouldQueue`; API resources must use `whenLoaded()`, `whenCounted()`, conditional fields, pagination, sensitive-column filtering, and query-count tests for important endpoints.
- Test performance-sensitive changes with focused Pest coverage for query counts, cache invalidation, visibility states, lazy-loading prevention, queue dispatch, and Livewire state/payload behavior.
- Deployment checklist: production uses `APP_ENV=production`, `APP_DEBUG=false`, `composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader`, production Vite assets, `php artisan optimize`, queue/long-running service reloads when active, OPcache reset on shared hosting, and no exposed Telescope, Debugbar, or verbose query logging.
